UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventnightmareoneaststreet26213-20261031@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261031T154208Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261031
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
SUMMARY:Nightmare on East Street
DESCRIPTION:We’re bringing a full day of Halloween thrills to Sandbox! 1:00 PM - 6:00 PM | Flash Tattoos: Kick off the day with some real\, permanent body art! Charli and Caitlin from Blue Crab Tattoo will be on-site slinging spooky season flash tattoos. 6:00 PM - Midnight | Live Music: Stick around for an ultra-talented\, thematic lineup featuring The Portside Chapel\, Vacant Windows\, Stainless Steve\, The Fato Company\, and Tenth Frame\, presented by Brain Dead Live! Plus\, browse frightfully wonderful goods from local vendors around the taproom! Oh\, we’re also giving the patio a Halloween makeover for the day. There is a $10 cover starting at 5:45PM. Don’t forget to wear your costume! It is Halloween\, isn’t it??
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/nightmare-on-east-street/26213/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventspooktoberfest26298-20261031@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261031T154208Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261031
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
SUMMARY:Spooktober Fest
DESCRIPTION:SPOOKTOBER FEST IS HERE! Get ready for the ultimate autumn crossover: Oktoberfest meets Halloween this Saturday starting at 12:00 PM! We’re kicking off the day with: Bier Garden: Cold Hofbräu flowing on tap all day long. $6 pints of Hofbräu - $12 Stein refills Fest Bites: Juicy brats and warm\, soft Bavarian pretzels. Spooky Cocktail Specials: Wicked brews for those craving something extra festive! Stein Hoisting Competition (3:00 PM): Test your strength for supreme bragging rights and prizes. Do you have what it takes to hold the stein the longest? Grab your friends\, throw on a costume or your dirndl & lederhosen\, and join us for food\, drinks\, and a spooktacular time! When: Saturday | 12 PM Stein Hoisting: Starts sharp at 3 PM
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/spooktober-fest/26298/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventthehoudinisc3a9ance26087-20261031@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261031T154208Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261031
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
SUMMARY:The Houdini Séance
DESCRIPTION:Step beyond the veil for a spine-chilling evening of mystery\, history\, and the supernatural. Hosted inside the ultra-intimate Frederick Magic Theater & Lounge\, The Houdini Séance invites you to take a seat at the table for an authentic re-creation of the legendary dark séances of the 1920s. Harry Houdini spent his final years challenging the afterlife and exposing fraudulent mediums—yet he left behind a secret code\, promising his wife Bess that he would escape the grave if it were humanly possible. Tonight\, we put that promise to the test. Frederick Magic Theater & Lounge is an Age 21+ venue. Please note that our historic building requires guests to use stairs to reach theater seating. We do not have an elevator or ramp available.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/the-houdini-s%c3%a9ance/26087/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventbackfromthedeadindoorperformanceallsaintsday22449-20261101@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261031T154208Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Back from the Dead Indoor Performance - All Saints Day
DESCRIPTION:The dead would like to have some words with you...the question of the night is: are you ready for your death? This is the indoor version of our Cemetery Walk.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/back-from-the-dead-indoor-performance-all-saints-day/22449/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventdayofthedead26287-20261101@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261031T154208Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Day of the Dead
DESCRIPTION:Join The Radical for a celebration of Día de Muertos (Day of the Dead)\, a Mexican tradition that brings family\, friends\, and communities together to remember and honor loved ones who have passed\, while celebrating the joy of life and the memories that keep their spirits alive. We're bringing together craft cocktails\, delicious Mexican food from La Carreta Tortas y Tacos\, music\, and family-friendly activities for an afternoon and evening of food\, drink\, remembrance\, and community. What to expect: Craft cocktails from The Radical\, including special Día de Muertos-inspired offerings alongside our regular favorites. Authentic Mexican food from La Carreta\, serving up delicious food to enjoy throughout the celebration. Music and a festive atmosphere to bring people together throughout the day and evening. Family-friendly themed activities inspired by the colors\, creativity\, and traditions of Día de Muertos. A chance to gather and remember\, celebrating the people\, stories\, and connections that remain with us. Whether you're familiar with Día de Muertos traditions or discovering them for the first time\, we invite you to join us in celebrating the rich cultural heritage behind this occasion and the universal importance of remembering those who came before us. Bring your friends\, bring your family\, and come spend some time with your neighbors as we celebrate life\, memory\, and community in the heart of Brunswick.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/day-of-the-dead/26287/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgevent2026exhibitsatmuseumoffrederickcountyhistory24908-20261105@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261031T154208Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261105
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261106
SUMMARY:2026 Exhibits at Museum of Frederick County History
DESCRIPTION:Take a deep dive into various topics that have defined Frederick's history\, as we celebrate America's 250th anniversary and our County's role in the Revolution. Featuring brand new exhibits: Cultivating Independence: Frederick in the Revolution Witnessing Revolution All Saints Street: Avenue to the History of Frederick and Its African American Community Growing Gold: A History of Frederick’s Goldfish Industry And returning favorites: Etchison Connections Timeless Toys 24 E Church Street Decorative Arts See our all new and renovated exhibits\, March 7\,2026 through December 12\, 2026. Buy tickets here.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/2026-exhibits-at-museum-of-frederick-county-history/24908/
END:VEVENT
